# Build and run only on request

Do not compile, build, install, or run the project (or its tests, examples, scripts, premake, make, `./bin/llae`, etc.) unless the user **explicitly** asks in the current message.

## Default behavior

- After code changes: describe what to run and why; do not execute it.
- Do not run builds or tests to "verify" changes on your own.
- Do not start servers, long-running processes, or background jobs unless asked.

## When it is allowed

Only when the user clearly requests it, for example:

- "build the project", "run tests", "run ./bin/llae run tests"
- "check that it compiles"
- "build and fix errors"

If the request is ambiguous (e.g. "check it"), ask whether they want a build/run or a static review.

## Still allowed without explicit ask

- Read/search files and grep the codebase
- Edit files
- Git read-only commands (`git status`, `git diff`, `git log`) when needed for the task
- Other non-executing investigation tools
